nickel@milton.u.washington.edu (Robert DeLoura) writes:
 If you already know where the staircase is, which was mentioned as a
 requirement, how does the ability to type ">" or "<" instead of "kkkjjjjjlllkk
 kklllllkkkhhhhhhh" make the game any easier?

There are two problems here

1) When do you "know" where the stairs are?

   You don't know, I believe, until you have actually traversed the
   stairs.  Just seeing them isn't good enough.  It's possible to see
   something that looks like stairs, but really isn't.

2) What do you do when there are more than one?  There are some levels
   that have more than one up-stairwell (or ladder, as the case may be),
   for example.  How do you pick which one to jump to?

   I guess you could keep typing ">" until you got to the one you
   wanted.  This all assumes you can teleport on such a level, but one
   needs to think about these situations, just in case...

Other than that, I like the idea.

Of course, once you add a couple shorthands, folks will want more: "I
wanna type '_' to get to my altar", "I wanna type '{' to jump to a
fountain"; "I wanna"....

